        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:06 a.m.\nAPPEARANCES:\nRICHARD M. SUMMA, ESQ., Tallahassee, Florida; on behalf of the Petitioner.\nJONATHAN C. BOND, Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Richard M. Summa (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2019-18-6662",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9be2d070391ddf0acfa0e298bfa054407bbc8516324458b52c377539bb625ed9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9be2d070391d-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SUMMA: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court:\nMr. Shular has prior convictions for drug offenses lacking the mens rea element necessary to distinguish between blameworthy and otherwise innocent conduct.\nIn 1986, one state, North Dakota, had dispensed with the element of guilty knowledge for its drug trafficking crimes. Today, Florida is the only state lacking a guilty knowledge element. Florida's law is an aberration.\nThe question here is whether Congress intended convictions under such an aberrational law to support the extreme sentencing enhancement of up to life in prison under ACCA.\nThe answer is no for a variety of reasons."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2019-18-6662",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9be2d070391ddf0acfa0e298bfa054407bbc8516324458b52c377539bb625ed9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9be2d070391d-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: But have I got the issue right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-18-6662",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9be2d070391ddf0acfa0e298bfa054407bbc8516324458b52c377539bb625ed9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9be2d070391d-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: We're told that, under Florida law, you could have a pretty low level offense, we just heard that, and -- and have a 15-year maximum."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-18-6662",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9be2d070391ddf0acfa0e298bfa054407bbc8516324458b52c377539bb625ed9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9be2d070391d-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: What is the --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-18-6662",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9be2d070391ddf0acfa0e298bfa054407bbc8516324458b52c377539bb625ed9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9be2d070391d-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Mr. Bond, do you think Congress intended to criminalize a mailman's delivery or Postal Service delivery?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2019-18-6662",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9be2d070391ddf0acfa0e298bfa054407bbc8516324458b52c377539bb625ed9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9be2d070391d-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: How do you draw -- how do you draw the line he's referring to?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-18-6662",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9be2d070391ddf0acfa0e298bfa054407bbc8516324458b52c377539bb625ed9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9be2d070391d-0002-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And, by the way, those elements, everywhere but Florida, require the prosecution to come in -- you've heard the argument -- and -- and to show that he knew that this powder was heroin."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2019-18-6662",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9be2d070391ddf0acfa0e298bfa054407bbc8516324458b52c377539bb625ed9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9be2d070391d-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "He agrees, at reply brief page 7, with our interpretation of it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2019-18-6662",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9be2d070391ddf0acfa0e298bfa054407bbc8516324458b52c377539bb625ed9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9be2d070391d-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Yeah, and just to put a friendly amendment to that, I don't mean to prolong it, but \"involve\" has to end somewhere along the chain, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-18-6662",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9be2d070391ddf0acfa0e298bfa054407bbc8516324458b52c377539bb625ed9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9be2d070391d-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: If Congress had before it when it drafted this provision of ACCA these two models, the federal model where the prosecution has to prove that guilty knowledge of the nature of the substance, and the Florida model, which differs only in that the defendant has to raise this as a -- an affirmative defense, has to say I didn't know that it was an"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-18-6662",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9be2d070391ddf0acfa0e298bfa054407bbc8516324458b52c377539bb625ed9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9be2d070391d-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Is there any practical difference between those two? I -- I mean, I don't see it. I don't think very many people are going to get -- get acquitted under the federal law unless they're willing to stand up and say I didn't know this was cocaine, in which case the two things are exactly the same."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2019-18-6662",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9be2d070391ddf0acfa0e298bfa054407bbc8516324458b52c377539bb625ed9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9be2d070391d-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted. (Whereupon, at 11:07 a.m. the case was submitted.)"
    },
